  "releaseNotes": "- Fix `TextConversions.AsDateTime` and `TextConversions.AsDateTimeOffset` to return `None` (instead of throwing `ArgumentOutOfRangeException`) when a `/Date(...)/` value overflows the valid `DateTime`/`DateTimeOffset` range; use `InvariantCulture` explicitly when parsing the milliseconds value\n- Fix error message in Range header validation: show the original header value (not the internal byte array representation) when the range format is invalid",
